text:
mira: opened a small docs PR to standardize streaming pagination snippets across py/ts/go. primary focus: resumable resume_token pattern, non-blocking retries, and a short migration note about TTLs. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/940
jess: quick ask: for TS please include both `for await` and an EventEmitter style. some frontends still prefer evented APIs.
raf: also recommend we show a tiny dedupe pattern (in-memory set) and warn that token IDs may change across model versions.
mira: added compact examples. python snippet uses our async retry helper and avoids blocking sleeps:
```python
# python: async streaming + resume + non-blocking retry
seen = set()
async for page in client.responses.stream_paginate(prompt, resume_token=None):
    for tok in page.tokens:
        if tok.id in seen:
            continue
        handle(tok)
        seen.add(tok.id)
    # persist latest resume token (short TTL)
    await kv.put('resume_token', page.resume_token)
    if page.transient_error:
        await retry_with_jitter(lambda: client.responses.resume(page.resume_token))
```
jess: nice. TS examples look good. generator + emitter included. I left a tiny types suggestion for the emitter payload.
```ts
// ts: async generator
for await (const page of client.responses.streamPaginate({ prompt })) {
  page.tokens.forEach(t => handleToken(t))
}
// ts: emitter style
const em = client.responses.streamPaginateEmitter({ prompt })
em.on('page', page => page.tokens.forEach(t => { if (!seen.has(t.id)) { handle(t); seen.add(t.id) }}))
em.on('error', async (e) => {
  if (e.code === 'ExpiredResumeToken') { /* restart from scratch */ }
  else if (e.type === 'Transient') { await retryWithJitter(() => client.responses.resume(e.resume_token)) }
})
```
raf: pushed a tiny gofmt fix for the Go snippet. Go sample uses a cancellable context and a channel consumer plus a map-based dedupe. also added a note to respect rate-limit headers before retrying aggressively.
ci-bot: link-checker: 3/3 links OK. docs-lint: one long line in TS example (wrapped).
mira: wrapped line and added a short migration blurb: "resume_token is preferred for streaming; offsets can break on sharded backends. resume_tokens may expire behind load-balancers—detect ExpiredResumeToken and restart gracefully." added CHANGELOG line "docs: unify streaming pagination snippets across SDKs" and will backport to release/v1.8 as docs-only.
jess: LGTM, small nit about naming 'resume_token' vs 'cursor' — choose one consistently.
raf: unified to 'resume_token' throughout.
mira: merging after CI. I'll post a short note to #integrations and open a follow-up issue to add an end-to-end reconnect example in the examples repo. thanks!
